cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PICSP3D in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PICSP3D: a parallel three-dimensional electrostatic particle-in-cell code for plasma-object interaction"
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23932321
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23932321
    description: "Zenodo archive of version 3.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sayanadhikari/picsp"
abstract: >-
  PICSP3D is an open-source 3D3V electrostatic particle-in-cell code for plasma-object
  interaction. Objects of arbitrary shape, from analytic primitives or CAD (STL), are embedded
  in a uniform grid with second-order cut-cell boundaries and charged self-consistently as
  floating or biased conductors. It includes secondary electron emission, photoemission with
  self-shadowing, static uniform and spatially varying magnetic fields, Monte Carlo collisions
  with a neutral background and binary Coulomb collisions, and is parallelised with MPI and
  OpenMP.
keywords:
  - particle-in-cell
  - plasma simulation
  - spacecraft charging
  - plasma-object interaction
  - embedded boundaries
  - Monte Carlo collisions
  - MPI
  - OpenMP
